WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.219 --> 00:00:01.728
- [Narrator] Let's say
you're a cheese producer,

00:00:01.728 --> 00:00:03.789
and you need a loan because
you want to buy a tractor

00:00:03.789 --> 00:00:06.579
or food for your cows or
really just about anything.

00:00:06.579 --> 00:00:09.048
There's a bank in Italy
that will take your cheese

00:00:09.048 --> 00:00:10.059
and give you cash.

00:00:10.059 --> 00:00:11.408
This is the story of three men

00:00:11.408 --> 00:00:13.579
and millions of dollars worth of cheese.

00:00:13.579 --> 00:00:16.496
(light soft music)

00:00:18.779 --> 00:00:19.612
Meet Mauro.

00:00:19.612 --> 00:00:20.777
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:20.777 --> 00:00:23.548
He's a cheese producer in
the Emiliano region of Italy.

00:00:23.548 --> 00:00:25.465
He produces Parmigiano-Reggiano,

00:00:25.465 --> 00:00:27.468
the so called “King of Cheese.”

00:00:27.468 --> 00:00:31.551
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:34.797 --> 00:00:35.630
(record scratching)

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.580
20,000 wheels? Holy cow,
that's a lot of cheese.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.100
When Mauro or another cheese producer

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:41.798
in this part of Italy needs a loan,

00:00:41.798 --> 00:00:45.129
they go to Credito Emiliano,
a big Italian bank.

00:00:45.129 --> 00:00:46.268
And like any bank,

00:00:46.268 --> 00:00:48.666
Credito Emiliano needs
collateral for their loan.

00:00:48.666 --> 00:00:51.174
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:53.204
And to do that, he talks to Fausto.

00:00:53.204 --> 00:00:54.037
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:00:54.037 --> 00:00:55.667
He works for Credito Emiliano.

00:00:55.667 --> 00:00:59.750
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:03.031 --> 00:01:04.978
Parmigiano-Reggiano is
a special kind of cheese

00:01:04.978 --> 00:01:07.450
because it needs to be
aged for 18 to 36 months

00:01:07.450 --> 00:01:10.030
and a wheel can be worth
thousands of dollars.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:12.031
Making it a safe long term
investment for the bank.

00:01:12.031 --> 00:01:16.114
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:27.739 --> 00:01:29.511
To be clear, the bank doesn't
store the valuable cheese

00:01:29.511 --> 00:01:32.092
in its vaults next to gold
bars and stacks of cash.

00:01:32.092 --> 00:01:34.151
They have a special cheese
warehouse down the road

00:01:34.151 --> 00:01:37.831
filled with thousands and
thousands of wheels of cheese.

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.148
That's where Roberto comes in.

00:01:39.148 --> 00:01:42.290
He's the general director of the
Tagliate General Warehouses.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:44.639
That's where Credito
Emiliano stores their cheese.

00:01:44.639 --> 00:01:47.970
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:48.803
Roberto and his team

00:01:48.803 --> 00:01:50.990
take care of more than
300,000 wheels of cheese

00:01:50.990 --> 00:01:54.071
that's currently worth more
than 160 million euros.

00:01:54.071 --> 00:01:56.665
Without proper care, the cheese
could lose it's value.

00:01:56.665 --> 00:02:00.748
(speaking in a foreign language)

00:02:04.879 --> 00:02:07.219
Well Roberto, sounds to
me like the cow, the bank

00:02:07.219 --> 00:02:09.668
and the cheese are in good hands.

00:02:09.668 --> 00:02:12.668
(light soft music)

